# Implementation plans

A plan breaks a feature that needs more than one PR into phases that each ship on
their own. Plans are written for AI agents and people alike: the agent workflow
(`/plan-tech`, `/prep`, `/build`; see [docs/CONTRIBUTING.md](../docs/CONTRIBUTING.md))
creates and follows them.

The guides (`CLAUDE.md`, each area's `Agents.md`) outrank a plan. If a plan
contradicts them, the guides win and the plan gets corrected.

## Layout

```
.implementation_plans/
  <plan-name>/                 kebab-case, no "plan" in the name
    README.md                  overview, phase tracker, stories, dependencies, out of scope
{%- if tracker == "none" %}
    STORIES.md                 the stories and their acceptance criteria (IDs S1, S2, ...)
{%- endif %}
    phase-1-<slug>.md          one document per phase
    phase-2-<slug>.md
  DONE/<version>/<plan-name>/  finished plans, filed under the release that shipped them
```

## Plan README

Front matter, then these sections: Status, Overview, Phase tracker (phase, size,
status), Stories (which phase finishes each story), Dependencies, Out of scope,
Security notes, Related docs.

```yaml
---
plan: <plan-name>
{%- if tracker == "linear" %}
project: <Linear project UUID>
{%- elif tracker == "github" %}
epic: <GitHub issue number of the epic>
{%- else %}
stories: STORIES.md
{%- endif %}
---
```

## Phase documents

Each phase is roughly 300-1000 changed lines and leaves the product working.

```yaml
---
phase_id: 1
title: Notes API
{%- if tracker == "linear" %}
implements: [{{ tracker_key }}-12, {{ tracker_key }}-13]
{%- elif tracker == "github" %}
implements: [12, 13]
{%- else %}
implements: [S1, S2]
{%- endif %}
depends_on: []          # direct dependencies only
domain: backend         # backend | frontend | ui-kit | fullstack | infra | docs
estimated_size: M       # S (< 300 lines) | M (300-700) | L (700-1000)
---
```

Sections: Status, Required reading, Goal, Deliverables (numbered and testable),
Verifiability checklist (commands), Security checklist, Implementation notes,
Acceptance criteria, Hand-off to the next phase, Deferred items.

## Lifecycle

1. Status `Draft` while planning, `Ready` after `/prep` passes, `In progress`, then `Done`.
2. A merged PR must leave its phase marked `Done` in the phase doc and the README tracker.
3. When every phase is done, move the folder to `DONE/<version>/` in the release that
   shipped it.
